        component; that was WRONG and is corrected here -- the "zlib" evidence
        turned out to be `#include <zlib.h>`, i.e. a dependency on zlib, not a
        licence grant covering Highly Experimental itself.
Notice: DELETED 2026-08-01, along with the Sony BIOS image it required. The
        engine could not initialise without a real Sony PlayStation 2 BIOS:
        HEPlugin::fromFile() loaded data/hebios.bin, passed it to
        bios_set_image(), and returned nullptr if it was absent. That file was
        512 KB of Sony Computer Entertainment firmware -- it contains the
        literal string "Copyright 1999-2002 (C) Sony Computer Entertainment
        Inc." -- and it was shipping inside BOTH bundles at
        Contents/Resources/data/hebios.bin, with no entry in this file. It is
        not ours to redistribute under any licence or on any store, so it was
        removed (both copies: data/hebios.bin and the unreferenced duplicate at
        external/musicplayer/data/hebios.bin). With the BIOS gone the plugin
        could not decode anything in any variant, and an unlicensed engine that
        plays nothing is pure liability, so the plugin was deleted outright
        rather than kept behind a build gate.
        NO SONGS WERE LOST. PSF1/PSF2 playback moved to AOSDK's BIOS-free HLE
        engines, above; verified over ~100 modland rips with
        `cm --dump-metadata` -- every file Highly Experimental could load, AOSDK
        loads. The rips that fail fail under BOTH engines, for a reason that is
        neither engine's fault: their "_lib2" tags name companion libraries with
        underscores that modland stores with spaces.
        A second, equally unlicensed copy of this engine still sits unused and
        UNCOMPILED at external/zxtune/3rdparty/he/ -- it arrived with the zxtune
        vendor drop, is referenced only by an upstream app subdirectory this
        project does not build, and reaches neither binary.

